{%- comment -%}
  Free gift above a cart value
  ----------------------------
  Adds a gift product to the cart when the spend on the other items reaches a threshold,
  removes it when the cart drops below, and keeps its quantity at 1.
  If the customer removes the gift themselves, it is not added back for the rest of the visit.

  The script only manages the cart line. The price must be made 0 by Shopify itself, with an
  automatic discount (Buy X get Y: minimum purchase amount -> the gift product, 100% off),
  so checkout stays correct even with JavaScript disabled. See docs/free-gift-setup.md.

  Render once, in layout/theme.liquid before </body>:
    {% render 'free-gift-threshold', gift_handle: 'free-tote-bag', threshold: 5000 %}

  Parameters:
  - gift_handle        handle of the gift product
  - threshold          amount in the store's default currency, in major units (5000 = 5,000.00)
  - refresh_sections   optional, which theme sections to re-render after the script changes the cart
                       (format "section-id:#selector,section-id:#selector"; the default matches Dawn)

  To switch the offer off, set the gift product to Draft: the script is not output at all.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gift_product = all_products[gift_handle]
  assign gift_variant = gift_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign threshold_cents = threshold | times: 100
  assign refresh_sections = refresh_sections | default: 'cart-drawer:#CartDrawer,cart-icon-bubble:#cart-icon-bubble'
-%}

{%- if gift_variant and gift_variant.available and threshold_cents > 0 -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="free-gift-config">
    {
      "variantId": {{ gift_variant.id }},
      "threshold": {{ threshold_cents }},
      "refreshSections": {{ refresh_sections | json }}
    }
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'free-gift-threshold.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
